Subject: [PATCH] build: Disable unversioned ABI warning, -Wchkp and -Wsuggest-attribute=const

GCC 11 diagnoses bare -Wabi because the default ABI has nothing to warn
about.  With -Werror this prevents even make-prime-list from compiling.
Exclude it from the optional warning set without disabling -Werror.

-Wchkp is also no longer supported by ppc-amigaos-gcc; gnulib's manywarn
probe doesn't reject it (the compiler only emits a driver warning, not
an error), so it ends up enabled and prints
"warning: switch '-Wchkp' is no longer supported" on every compile.
Disable it the same way.

-Wsuggest-attribute=const is advisory and depends on which branches of
a function dead-code-eliminate on a given platform; on this target it
fires on lib/physmem.c's physmem_total/physmem_available (which reduce
to a single fallback return here, since none of their recognized memory
APIs exist on AmigaOS):

lib/physmem.c:85:1: error: function might be candidate for attribute 'const' [-Werror=suggest-attribute=const]

Disable it rather than patch every function gnulib reduces differently
per platform.

Update generated configure as well for builds that do not run Autoconf.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -114,6 +114,9 @@
   # This, $nw, is the list of warnings we disable.
   nw="$nw -Wdeclaration-after-statement" # too useful to forbid
   nw="$nw -Waggregate-return"       # anachronistic
+  nw="$nw -Wabi"
+  nw="$nw -Wchkp"                   # no longer supported by ppc-amigaos-gcc
+  nw="$nw -Wsuggest-attribute=const" # too platform-dependent (lib/physmem.c)
   nw="$nw -Wlong-long"              # C90 is anachronistic (lib/gethrxtime.h)
   nw="$nw -Wc++-compat"             # We don't care about C++ compilers
   nw="$nw -Wundef"                  # Warns on '#if GNULIB_FOO' etc in gnulib
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -64376,6 +64376,9 @@
   # This, $nw, is the list of warnings we disable.
   nw="$nw -Wdeclaration-after-statement" # too useful to forbid
   nw="$nw -Waggregate-return"       # anachronistic
+  nw="$nw -Wabi"
+  nw="$nw -Wchkp"                   # no longer supported by ppc-amigaos-gcc
+  nw="$nw -Wsuggest-attribute=const" # too platform-dependent (lib/physmem.c)
   nw="$nw -Wlong-long"              # C90 is anachronistic (lib/gethrxtime.h)
   nw="$nw -Wc++-compat"             # We don't care about C++ compilers
   nw="$nw -Wundef"                  # Warns on '#if GNULIB_FOO' etc in gnulib
